#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e11a1f-00dc-51de-8fae-8e31288e9455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515155} {:answer/id #uuid "98af0664-fef3-5195-8942-4ae62f79f459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515196} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3d9aa4-b230-5307-8b9e-8fda1b89d36a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 3\\,,\\,2x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515211} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a1af78-5337-58fe-9506-fb9b3db058f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le 2\\,,\\,2x\\le y\\le (x-1)^{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515222} {:answer/id #uuid "f038c740-7bd9-542c-aa85-3c158363caa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f038c740-7bd9-542c-aa85-3c158363caa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515376} :answer-field/id #uuid "121eed80-0cfa-5e17-b370-61189884e2ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "771776cb-495a-5541-85ae-ed89a3b38002" :question/math-academy-id "q-71830" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7a556f986c44b922908b79e3982e098eb7250d9d470092ba2c45bbffe190913.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=2x\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2}\n$$\n\nThe function $x=\\sqrt{y}+1$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=4.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 4.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/c5/c55d5f809462b767122ccc4af97c5b4d243730ed24f655bdc18e35ec57e25ce2.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=\\frac{y}{2}$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\sqrt{y}+1.$ So, we have $\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129842 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55a6ee0a-d96f-565a-b86b-753fef10bcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460173} {:answer/id #uuid "c5fa2d01-0363-5414-aee0-15a329ab0bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55a6ee0a-d96f-565a-b86b-753fef10bcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460173} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ad56762-b330-5bb1-8ba0-9869f5af2ead" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460953} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3f634cf-ea4c-5e68-b5da-4eef1c1c56af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460175} {:answer/id #uuid "49f35556-5b7c-515b-9a7a-4189930ec2c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3f634cf-ea4c-5e68-b5da-4eef1c1c56af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460175} :answer-field/id #uuid "409900db-4264-516b-b459-9b27a44721c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ae5851-54cb-53e1-a0fe-3cb10c69a3f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460177} {:answer/id #uuid "58d69edb-8d2a-5ce7-bef1-d0329b4c1d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d69edb-8d2a-5ce7-bef1-d0329b4c1d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460178} :answer-field/id #uuid "f764f310-ac1b-5163-8ef9-b2f704f3384e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7805c1fc-f8dc-58be-9c44-d22a8226c755" :question/math-academy-id "q-71895" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/24/24cbd9a0e01023dca6a289838d94efe3c7b67abe5b7a1f275f6945f280e65d64.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.75$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/6c/6c51abe5c21571a9c5596fce4e3b8ace210eacfab125016e6b9a3b2a7bc2e056.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/f9/f9fed5856eda128d84debec320bc38a35eaa2bf5184b1f81cb1194b02f8a306a.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd4804dc-232f-5717-b07c-b3e74fbff1bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375323} {:answer/id #uuid "a9fa7755-b5ce-5247-a0a8-910a9073e68d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ef/ef9d0a612a093852fd9f60fb20c86b946c178f9e2a9877ef7c16f89f98e324f6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375324} {:answer/id #uuid "89301be4-f9a9-59a2-ac5e-5d39c6146fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/67/67b42d8a49263abc8cce98f20b59370047b989ae69d55050e4001897ba3f9d2e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375325} {:answer/id #uuid "0e509b6d-02de-56c1-a9e8-7efb98174520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5e/5eb14fb126d8b0df54e5523d705cb5491e161c00b118f07a0bf3407644b7d4a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375326} {:answer/id #uuid "79d18367-2462-5b79-ac87-734c517ed764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/3228d2d0c2fb3ce74c98b018c0694e9da5fc4a8444a7b67b5fb7fa0eb24eaa6c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e509b6d-02de-56c1-a9e8-7efb98174520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5e/5eb14fb126d8b0df54e5523d705cb5491e161c00b118f07a0bf3407644b7d4a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375326} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d8d4731-859f-5217-921a-45bb7148c36f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f280067d-2410-589e-b620-7c39e01b3ccd" :question/math-academy-id "q-72319" :question/problem "Which of the following is a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/12/1206abdf317df09c8c54714a6178d78570b3c10a49513c3c626c09be3ea2cf72.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Type II Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1756c48c-665f-5f06-b577-1b909cc87f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+3\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}+2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514921} {:answer/id #uuid "1a8d8801-ef97-55e2-bc3a-31cf1be29d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\sqrt{y}\\le y\\le \\frac{y}{2},\\,1\\le x\\le 3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514930} {:answer/id #uuid "a8039587-077a-5341-9003-3971e08c6ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515225} {:answer/id #uuid "b4fa72f4-3cd9-588c-8d31-a887a4ecafd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le y\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3,\\,1\\le x\\le 3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515251} {:answer/id #uuid "f6ff3e83-5d71-5daa-b2f8-25c47f45a202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le 2.5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8039587-077a-5341-9003-3971e08c6ca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515225} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dd26fe5-df42-54f1-a759-c32dddc997da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80f56e91-1777-5d7a-b918-7d315f6b332a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73534" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c316b62d5c1a08c6513413fd87c36c6feb26fb632709909a9c9f761d0806c4af.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-2(x-3)\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{y}{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe function $x=-\\sqrt{y}+2$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=3.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/fb/fb05eec73599c1beb8dd588c478208315f6edaf10af999115eb29fa10d5601e9.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=-\\sqrt{y}+2$ and leaves through the upper function $x=-\\frac{y}{2}+3.$ So, we have $-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129169 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Region as Type I, Type II, Both, or Neither"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c94e30f0-68f2-5998-b9f9-644e9e44b95f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468070} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0ed006-c485-5f47-9cb3-66d73cb5b6eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c94e30f0-68f2-5998-b9f9-644e9e44b95f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468070} :answer-field/id #uuid "e579a2ca-789a-528f-993a-72fedc592395" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5794e6f7-e7be-5b7e-8bb8-bb34003ae429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468072} {:answer/id #uuid "c1777e06-539e-50b4-a94c-4208586ed294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5794e6f7-e7be-5b7e-8bb8-bb34003ae429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468072} :answer-field/id #uuid "3694904e-0ccc-5a31-b8a9-6ec58e4eec46" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6117a2a3-4603-5502-8e5e-e303e66ecd3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468074} {:answer/id #uuid "32f5d350-119e-5636-b3cb-0f999c5e3d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32f5d350-119e-5636-b3cb-0f999c5e3d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468075} :answer-field/id #uuid "abcdcfba-e886-55b6-abf8-403802e888af" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "451e02c3-10e2-5101-a83f-538a8be6b03d" :question/math-academy-id "q-73549" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the ellipses $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/62/627e7e102a0f16cb0c4946e42b48ad122299d729c5bc419293e258a3f2e1701e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/d7/d7aa48c887d6fb1c3d0420867b7e74010fa93e16d7e24317e2cf214764e56113.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/ec/ec632fa5f86d8d9b34b9ccf661a3219e965f289c28bf69d7d80eeeb46093e7ae.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}]}
